  triage:title "duplicate ACCEPT_POLL_INTERVAL constant" ;
  triage:description "duplicate ACCEPT_POLL_INTERVAL constant re-declared in more than one location as a side effect of this round's RULE-003 decomposition of local_ipc_transport.rs. UDS polls 1ms at local_ipc_transport.rs:53-57,777-782; TCP polls 1ms at local_tcp_transport.rs:71-75,177-208; Graft receiver polls 25ms at atm-core/src/graft.rs:35. Arch-ctm confirmed (2026-08-03T02:09:03Z) this is load-bearing: it is the portable replacement for dummy wake connections and must be kept on all transport paths. Deferred to 'local-HTTP constant unification' refactor (not in scope for fix/localipcwake-accept-interrupt)." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "followup_pass" ;
